          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "frāternus is built on frāter \"brother\" (EtymDB; Lewis & Short), which is inherited from a Proto-Indo-European word for \"brother\"; English brother is a cousin. English fraternal comes from it."
            }
          ]
        },
